---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PPNav from '../../components/PPNav.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Edward James — Strategic Advisor" theme="pp">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/rv.css" slot="head" />
  <PPNav active="about" />
  <main style="padding-top:5rem;background:#F9FAFB;min-height:100vh;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif">

    <div style="max-width:1280px;margin-inline:auto;padding:4rem 1.5rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5rem">

      <!-- Bio Hero -->
      <section>
        <div class="pp-about-hero" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:4rem;align-items:center">
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2rem">
            <div>
              <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4rem);font-weight:700;line-height:1.1;color:#111827;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:0 0 .375rem">Beyond the<br><em style="font-style:italic;color:#4B5563">Boardroom.</em></h1>
            </div>
            <p style="font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:500;color:#111827;line-height:1.65;margin:0;max-width:34rem">
              I believe that true authority isn't about having the loudest voice in the room. It's about having the clarity to see what others miss, and the discipline to execute when others hesitate.
            </p>
            <p style="font-size:1rem;color:#4B5563;line-height:1.75;margin:0;max-width:34rem">
              For over two decades, I've navigated the complex intersections of global finance, corporate strategy, and organizational psychology. My approach is rooted in a simple truth: businesses don't transform; the people within them do. I partner with executives not just to restructure their operations, but to recalibrate their vision.
            </p>
            <p style="font-size:1rem;color:#4B5563;line-height:1.75;margin:0;max-width:34rem">
              When you strip away the corporate jargon and the complex models, what remains is trust, decisiveness, and an unwavering commitment to outcomes. That is what I bring to every engagement.
            </p>
            <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:2rem;padding-top:.5rem">
              <div>
                <div style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827">London</div>
                <div style="font-size:.75rem;color:#6B7280;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em">Based In</div>
              </div>
              <div style="width:1px;height:3rem;background:#E5E7EB"></div>
              <div>
                <div style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827">Global</div>
                <div style="font-size:.75rem;color:#6B7280;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em">Operating</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div style="position:relative">
            <div style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/5;border-radius:2rem;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 25px 60px -15px rgba(0,0,0,.2);background:#F3F4F6">
              <img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/3184339/pexels-photo-3184339.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=800" alt="Edward James executive portrait" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;filter:grayscale(30%)" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Career Timeline -->
      <section>
        <div style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">
          <h2 style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0 0 .75rem">The Journey</h2>
          <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:#4B5563;margin:0">A narrative of strategic evolution, from early foundational roles to shaping global enterprise architecture.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="position:relative;border-left:1px solid #E5E7EB;margin-left:1rem;padding-left:2.5rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2rem">
          <!-- Timeline item 1 -->
          <div style="position:relative;background:#fff;padding:2.5rem;border-radius:1.5rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05)">
            <div style="position:absolute;left:-2.75rem;top:2.5rem;width:.875rem;height:.875rem;border-radius:50%;background:#fff;border:3px solid #111827"></div>
            <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;border-bottom:1px solid #F3F4F6;padding-bottom:1.25rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem">
              <h3 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0">The Foundation: Risk &amp; Reality</h3>
              <span style="font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:600;color:#4B5563;background:#F3F4F6;padding:.375rem .875rem;border-radius:9999px">1998 — 2005</span>
            </div>
            <p style="font-size:.9375rem;color:#4B5563;line-height:1.75;margin:0">My career began in the trenches of risk management at a Tier-1 investment bank during a period of unprecedented market volatility. It was here I learned that models are only as good as the assumptions behind them. I quickly transitioned from analyzing risk to advising on structural resilience, learning to identify the invisible fault lines in large organizations before they fractured.</p>
          </div>
          <!-- Timeline item 2 -->
          <div style="position:relative;background:#fff;padding:2.5rem;border-radius:1.5rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05)">
            <div style="position:absolute;left:-2.75rem;top:2.5rem;width:.875rem;height:.875rem;border-radius:50%;background:#fff;border:3px solid #111827"></div>
            <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;border-bottom:1px solid #F3F4F6;padding-bottom:1.25rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem">
              <h3 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0">The Pivot: Strategic Scaling</h3>
              <span style="font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:600;color:#4B5563;background:#F3F4F6;padding:.375rem .875rem;border-radius:9999px">2006 — 2015</span>
            </div>
            <p style="font-size:.9375rem;color:#4B5563;line-height:1.75;margin:0">Recognizing that true value creation happens at the intersection of strategy and execution, I moved into management consulting, eventually leading the M&amp;A integration practice at a global firm. During this decade, I oversaw the post-merger integration of over $40B in assets. The core lesson? Culture eats strategy for breakfast, but operational dysfunction eats them both. I developed proprietary frameworks for aligning disparate corporate cultures while maintaining operational momentum.</p>
          </div>
          <!-- Timeline item 3 -->
          <div style="position:relative;background:#fff;padding:2.5rem;border-radius:1.5rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05)">
            <div style="position:absolute;left:-2.75rem;top:2.5rem;width:.875rem;height:.875rem;border-radius:50%;background:#fff;border:3px solid #111827"></div>
            <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;border-bottom:1px solid #F3F4F6;padding-bottom:1.25rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem">
              <h3 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0">The Present: Boardroom Advisory</h3>
              <span style="font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:600;color:#4B5563;background:#F3F4F6;padding:.375rem .875rem;border-radius:9999px">2016 — Present</span>
            </div>
            <p style="font-size:.9375rem;color:#4B5563;line-height:1.75;margin:0">Today, I operate exclusively at the board and C-suite level. I established Nexus Group to provide unfiltered, high-stakes advisory without the overhead of traditional consulting models. My current focus is guiding legacy institutions through digital transformation and advising high-growth tech firms on sustainable enterprise scaling. I sit on the boards of three publicly traded companies, providing governance and strategic oversight.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Core Philosophy -->
      <section>
        <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:2.5rem">
          <h2 style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0 0 .75rem">Core Philosophy</h2>
          <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:#4B5563;margin:0">The non-negotiable principles that dictate how I operate, advise, and lead.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pp-philosophy-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1.5rem">
          <div style="background:#fff;padding:2.5rem;border-radius:1.5rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05)">
            <div style="width:3.5rem;height:3.5rem;background:#F3F4F6;border-radius:.875rem;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0 0 1rem">Unvarnished Truth</h3>
            <p style="font-size:.9375rem;color:#4B5563;line-height:1.7;margin:0">I am not hired to validate existing opinions. I am hired to identify blind spots and articulate the realities that internal teams are often too compromised to voice. Candor is my primary currency.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="background:#fff;padding:2.5rem;border-radius:1.5rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05)">
            <div style="width:3.5rem;height:3.5rem;background:#F3F4F6;border-radius:.875rem;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0 0 1rem">Execution Over Ideation</h3>
            <p style="font-size:.9375rem;color:#4B5563;line-height:1.7;margin:0">A brilliant strategy that cannot be executed is a failed strategy. Every framework I design is pressure-tested against the operational realities and cultural constraints of the organization.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="background:#fff;padding:2.5rem;border-radius:1.5rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05)">
            <div style="width:3.5rem;height:3.5rem;background:#F3F4F6;border-radius:.875rem;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0 0 1rem">Long-Term Viability</h3>
            <p style="font-size:.9375rem;color:#4B5563;line-height:1.7;margin:0">I refuse to optimize for short-term optics at the expense of long-term structural integrity. My recommendations are built to withstand market cycles, not just the next quarterly earnings call.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Media Appearances -->
      <section>
        <h2 style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0 0 2rem">Media &amp; Speaking</h2>
        <div class="pp-media-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:1.5rem">
          <div style="background:#fff;padding:1.75rem;border-radius:1.25rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05);display:flex;gap:1.25rem;align-items:flex-start">
            <div style="width:2.75rem;height:2.75rem;background:#F3F4F6;border-radius:.625rem;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-shrink:0">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="2"><rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="8" y1="21" x2="16" y2="21"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12" y2="21"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div style="font-size:.75rem;color:#4F46E5;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;margin-bottom:.375rem">Bloomberg Television</div>
              <h4 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0 0 .375rem">The New Architecture of Corporate Governance</h4>
              <p style="font-size:.875rem;color:#4B5563;margin:0">Featured segment on board structural reform in post-pandemic enterprises. March 2024.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div style="background:#fff;padding:1.75rem;border-radius:1.25rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05);display:flex;gap:1.25rem;align-items:flex-start">
            <div style="width:2.75rem;height:2.75rem;background:#F3F4F6;border-radius:.625rem;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-shrink:0">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="2"><path d="M3 9l9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/><polyline points="9 22 9 12 15 12 15 22"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div style="font-size:.75rem;color:#4F46E5;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;margin-bottom:.375rem">Financial Times</div>
              <h4 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0 0 .375rem">M&amp;A Integration: What the Data Reveals</h4>
              <p style="font-size:.875rem;color:#4B5563;margin:0">Contributed analysis on integration failure patterns. Published in FT Special Report. November 2023.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div style="background:#fff;padding:1.75rem;border-radius:1.25rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05);display:flex;gap:1.25rem;align-items:flex-start">
            <div style="width:2.75rem;height:2.75rem;background:#F3F4F6;border-radius:.625rem;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-shrink:0">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div style="font-size:.75rem;color:#4F46E5;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;margin-bottom:.375rem">World Economic Forum</div>
              <h4 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0 0 .375rem">Keynote: Rebuilding Trust in Corporate Institutions</h4>
              <p style="font-size:.875rem;color:#4B5563;margin:0">Annual Davos plenary session on the future of boardroom accountability. January 2024.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div style="background:#fff;padding:1.75rem;border-radius:1.25rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05);display:flex;gap:1.25rem;align-items:flex-start">
            <div style="width:2.75rem;height:2.75rem;background:#F3F4F6;border-radius:.625rem;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-shrink:0">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#111827" stroke-width="2"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"/><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div style="font-size:.75rem;color:#4F46E5;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;margin-bottom:.375rem">Harvard Business Review</div>
              <h4 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0 0 .375rem">When Boards Need to Intervene — And How</h4>
              <p style="font-size:.875rem;color:#4B5563;margin:0">Feature article on board intervention protocols during executive leadership crises. September 2023.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Education -->
      <section>
        <h2 style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0 0 2rem">Education Credentials</h2>
        <div class="pp-edu-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1.5rem">
          <div style="background:#fff;padding:2rem;border-radius:1.5rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05)">
            <div style="font-size:.75rem;color:#4F46E5;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;margin-bottom:.75rem">1996 – 1998</div>
            <h3 style="font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0 0 .375rem">Master of Business Administration</h3>
            <p style="font-size:.9375rem;font-weight:500;color:#4B5563;margin:0 0 .5rem">London Business School</p>
            <p style="font-size:.875rem;color:#6B7280;margin:0">Specialization in Corporate Strategy & Organizational Behavior. Graduated with Distinction.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="background:#fff;padding:2rem;border-radius:1.5rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05)">
            <div style="font-size:.75rem;color:#4F46E5;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;margin-bottom:.75rem">1992 – 1995</div>
            <h3 style="font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0 0 .375rem">Bachelor of Science, Economics</h3>
            <p style="font-size:.9375rem;font-weight:500;color:#4B5563;margin:0 0 .5rem">London School of Economics</p>
            <p style="font-size:.875rem;color:#6B7280;margin:0">First Class Honours. Thesis on capital market efficiency in emerging economies.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="background:#fff;padding:2rem;border-radius:1.5rem;border:1px solid #E5E7EB;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.05)">
            <div style="font-size:.75rem;color:#4F46E5;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;margin-bottom:.75rem">2010</div>
            <h3 style="font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:700;color:#111827;margin:0 0 .375rem">Executive Leadership Program</h3>
            <p style="font-size:.9375rem;font-weight:500;color:#4B5563;margin:0 0 .5rem">Harvard Business School</p>
            <p style="font-size:.875rem;color:#6B7280;margin:0">Advanced leadership and organizational behavior executive education program.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid #E5E7EB;padding:3rem 1.5rem;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif">
    <div style="max-width:1280px;margin-inline:auto;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1.5rem">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.625rem">
        <div style="width:2rem;height:2rem;background:#111827;border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:#fff;font-size:.6875rem;font-weight:700">EJ</div>
        <span style="font-size:.9375rem;font-weight:600;color:#111827">Edward James</span>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:2rem;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <span style="font-size:.875rem;color:#6B7280">&copy; 2025 Edward James.</span>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem">
          <a href="https://linkedin.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#6B7280;text-decoration:none" aria-label="LinkedIn">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M16 8a6 6 0 0 1 6 6v7h-4v-7a2 2 0 0 0-2-2 2 2 0 0 0-2 2v7h-4v-7a6 6 0 0 1 6-6z"/><rect x="2" y="9" width="4" height="12"/><circle cx="4" cy="4" r="2"/></svg>
          </a>
          <a href="https://twitter.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#6B7280;text-decoration:none" aria-label="Twitter">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M22 4s-.7 2.1-2 3.4c1.6 10-9.4 17.3-18 11.6 2.2.1 4.4-.6 6-2C3 15.5.5 9.6 3 5c2.2 2.6 5.6 4.1 9 4-.9-4.2 4-6.6 7-3.8 1.1 0 3-1.2 3-1.2z"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <style>
    @media (max-width: 767px) {
      .pp-about-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; }
      .pp-philosophy-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; }
      .pp-media-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; }
      .pp-edu-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
